{
 "meta": {
  "date": "2026-11-14",
  "agent": "F-47",
  "track": "track-c-discovery-engine",
  "claim": "First full decryption of Clarion .DAT record bodies (all 6 encrypted samples from sembiance clarionDatabase corpus), using the 2-byte per-file XOR keys cracked in F-39 with the body-phase model; bodies validated against the F-38 schema and yield readable 1989-1992 business data.",
  "sample_source": "sembiance.com/fileFormatSamples/document/clarionDatabase/ (re-fetched 2026-11-14 to /tmp only; sizes match F-38 census and F-39 metadata)",
  "keys_source": "results/format-re/clarion-dat/clarion-encryption-keys.json (F-39)",
  "schema_source": "results/format-re/clarion-dat/clarion-dat-format.md (F-38)",
  "bounds": "raw sample bytes kept in /tmp only; only derived facts committed here"
 },
 "mechanism_confirmed": {
  "model": "per-file 2-byte periodic XOR (k0,k1); plaintext = cipher XOR k0 at even keystream index, k1 at odd; keystream phase resets at: header body @0x04, each 27-byte field descriptor, each 19-B KEYSECT and 6-B KEYPART, picture/array sections; record slot = 5-byte rhd/rptr header stored CLEAR + body encrypted with phase reset to k0 at body byte 0",
  "evidence": [
   "with this model all 6 encrypted files satisfy F-38 header arithmetic: desc_end==offset and filesize==offset+numrecs*reclen (6/6), same as 43 plain files",
   "record-slot bytes 0-4 read CLEAR give rhd in {0x01,0x05} active / {0x11,0x15} deleted and rptr values that reproduce the GEORGEE freelist chain exactly (17 deleted slots == numdels 17)",
   "GEORGEX 68-char TEXT fields that fill the field completely end in letters ('d','y','w') under the model; the last body byte IS encrypted (raw 0x5e/0x43/0x4d = letter XOR k1 0x3a)",
   "HHCNTRL last byte decrypts to 0x70 'p' = HHC:REGISTERED; GEORGEA password field decrypts to 12 spaces (empty)",
   "alternating-phase control: wrong phase (k1 first) yields non-printable garbage throughout; whole-slot phase (repo decoder records()) would corrupt the clear rhd/rptr bytes"
  ]
 },
 "decimal_format_correction": {
  "finding": "F-38/F-39 read DECIMAL by dropping the LAST nibble; the evidence shows the pad nibble is LEADING: stored nibbles = (pad if total digits odd) + integer digits (decsig) + fraction digits (decdec); no sign nibble observed in these samples",
  "evidence": [
   "TAXRATE.DAT NJ TAX:RATE nibbles 00000700 (decsig 3, decdec 4) -> drop leading 0 -> digits 0000700 -> 000.0700 = 7.00% New Jersey sales tax; F-38 reading gives 000.0070",
   "HHNAMES.DAT slot 1 HHN:PHONE_NO nibbles 0000008044885506 -> 8044885506 = (804) 488-5506, Chesapeake VA - matches the record's own address 'Chesapeake, VA 23321'; F-38 reading gives 9-digit 804488550 (not a valid number)",
   "HHCNTRL.DAT HHC:POLICE/FIRE/AMBULANCE nibbles 0000000000000911 -> 911 (US emergency number); F-38 reading gave 091",
   "HHCNTRL.DAT HHC:DOCTOR -> 4542323, OTHERPHONE1 -> 4345678, OTHERPHONE2 -> 5456787 (7-digit local numbers)"
  ]
 },
 "validation": {
  "header_arithmetic": "6/6 encrypted + 3/3 plain re-fetched samples: desc_end==offset, filesize==offset+numrecs*reclen",
  "georgee_longs": "29/29 NTR:DATE values decode to valid calendar dates 1991-01-01..1991-05-19; 29/29 NTR:TIME values in 1..8640000 (07:39..22:26, all 1991 plausibility)",
  "default_times": "15/15 first-pattern time fields decode to 08:00:00.00 in / 12:00:00.00 lunch / 17:00:00.00 out; second/third patterns are 0 (empty) as stored",
  "deleted_slots": "rhd bit 0x10 works on decrypted bodies: GEORGEE 17 deleted slots (== numdels 17), HHNAMES 5 deleted slots; freelist chain from freerec 6 = 6->28->27->26->25->1->23->22->21->20->19->18->17->16->14->13->12 (17 slots, ends rptr 0)",
  "deleted_content": "REFUTES the expectation that GEORGEE deleted slots are empty/password-cleared: all 17 deleted slots retain fully readable, correctly decrypted bodies (titles, dates, times intact) - deletion is a soft delete (rhd bit + freelist rptr chain), body not wiped; same for HHNAMES deleted slots (incl. author's own test records)",
  "cross_file_integrity": "GEORGEX TXT:NTRYREC references only valid GEORGEE slots {2,3,4,5,7,8,9,10,11,15,24,29} (12 active entries) plus 0 (empty text slot 23, whose GEORGEE slot 23 is itself deleted); TXT:TEXTNUM is contiguous 1..n per entry - the two tables join into one journal"
 },
 "anomalies": {
  "default_last_byte": "DEFAULT.DAT: 300/301 body bytes decrypt consistently; the final file byte (raw 0x00) decrypts to 0xd8 under the model, making DEF:WD5OUTIME3 read -671088640 instead of 0 (F-39 published 0, i.e. treated that byte as clear). All 45 other LONG fields and all STRING fields are clean.",
  "genesoft_last_byte": "GENESOFT.DAT: 180/181 body bytes decrypt consistently; the final file byte (raw 0x20) decrypts to 0xf3, leaving a stray high-bit byte after GEN:WEXDJNBMK 'qawsedrft' + padding (F-39 published 'qawsedrft').",
  "pattern": "the two anomalous files share k1=0xc6 (d8c6, d3c6); the four clean files (3e3a x3, 5056) encrypt their final byte consistently. Interpretation open: per-driver-version trailing-byte handling (GENESOFT is the oldest file, 1989), or a clear EOF/flush byte. Affects exactly 1 byte per file; no other byte deviates."
 },
